{
  "id": "book-27",
  "checkpoint": 11,
  "title": "Arriving at North Peak",
  "summary": "O trem chega à estação de North Peak no sopé da montanha. Paul desembarca, respira o ar puro da serra e recebe orientações sobre a trilha local.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-27.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "The train gently slows down as it pulls into North Peak station. The conductor announces the final stop over the speaker system. Paul stands up, retrieves his backpack from the overhead rack, and steps out onto the quiet platform.\n\nThe mountain air is crisp and cool. Surrounded by towering pine trees and rocky slopes, the small wooden station feels peaceful. Paul walks into the main lobby, where a local guide reviews a large trail board.\n\n“Welcome to North Peak,” the guide says warmly. “Are you hiking up the main path?”\n\n“Yes, I plan to reach the base camp before sunset,” Paul answers.\n\n“Follow the blue markers along the forest edge,” the guide advises. “Carry enough water and stay on the main track.”\n\nPaul nods with gratitude, adjusts his gear, and takes his first step onto the mountain trail.",
